/* mxPort.mib: the 8 RW columns, all in the portConfig half of the MIB.
 *
 * They all probe portStatIndex.1, NOT the RO index column of their own table.
 * Despite carrying the delegated mxportdb/ prefix, portConfigIndex (.1.1.1.1)
 * and portConfigLinkUpDelayIndex (.1.3.1.1) are still answered in-master --
 * verified on the wire: a GET of either produces no AgentX traffic at all.
 * Probing them makes netsnmp_subtree_find() return the LOCAL subtree, and the
 * forward then hands the request to a non-AgentX handler while still reporting
 * success: wrong value types, scalars turning into noSuchInstance, and GETNEXT
 * looping inside the column (a whole-tree walk collapses from 193 to 13).
 * Only the portStat half of mxPort actually moved to ISS, so pick the probe
 * there. ISS registers mxPort as a single MIB (mxPortdb.h `mxPortEntry`), so
 * one portStat probe resolves to the registration covering these columns too.
 *
 * When adding a rule for another group: confirm the probe with a pcap on
 * lo:705 -- it must produce a Get-PDU. "snmpget returns a value" proves
 * nothing, because in-master answers too. */
